{"note":"Add a verb by appending one object to the verbs array — the page renders everything from this file. Conjugations store the verb form only; the page pairs it with the subject and handles je -> j' elision for speech.","pronouns":["je","tu","il/elle/on","nous","vous","ils/elles"],"tenses":[{"id":"present","kidHint":"talking about right now","label":"Présent"},{"id":"passe_compose","kidHint":"something already done","label":"Passé composé"},{"id":"futur","kidHint":"something that will happen","label":"Futur simple"}],"verbs":[{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"sera","ils/elles":"seront","je":"serai","nous":"serons","tu":"seras","vous":"serez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a été","ils/elles":"ont été","je":"ai été","nous":"avons été","tu":"as été","vous":"avez été"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"est","ils/elles":"sont","je":"suis","nous":"sommes","tu":"es","vous":"êtes"}},"english":"to be","group":"irregular","infinitive":"être","regular":false,"tip":"The most important verb in French — and totally irregular. Worth memorizing cold!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"aura","ils/elles":"auront","je":"aurai","nous":"aurons","tu":"auras","vous":"aurez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a eu","ils/elles":"ont eu","je":"ai eu","nous":"avons eu","tu":"as eu","vous":"avez eu"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"a","ils/elles":"ont","je":"ai","nous":"avons","tu":"as","vous":"avez"}},"english":"to have","group":"irregular","infinitive":"avoir","regular":false,"tip":"The second super-verb. It also helps build the passé composé for most other verbs!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"ira","ils/elles":"iront","je":"irai","nous":"irons","tu":"iras","vous":"irez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"est allé","ils/elles":"sont allés","je":"suis allé","nous":"sommes allés","tu":"es allé","vous":"êtes allé"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"va","ils/elles":"vont","je":"vais","nous":"allons","tu":"vas","vous":"allez"}},"english":"to go","group":"irregular","infinitive":"aller","regular":false,"tip":"In the passé composé, aller uses être — and the ending matches who went! A girl writes 'allée', a group writes 'allés'."},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"fera","ils/elles":"feront","je":"ferai","nous":"ferons","tu":"feras","vous":"ferez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a fait","ils/elles":"ont fait","je":"ai fait","nous":"avons fait","tu":"as fait","vous":"avez fait"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"fait","ils/elles":"font","je":"fais","nous":"faisons","tu":"fais","vous":"faites"}},"english":"to do, to make","group":"irregular","infinitive":"faire","regular":false,"tip":"Watch out for 'vous faites' — it looks odd but it's correct!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"parlera","ils/elles":"parleront","je":"parlerai","nous":"parlerons","tu":"parleras","vous":"parlerez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a parlé","ils/elles":"ont parlé","je":"ai parlé","nous":"avons parlé","tu":"as parlé","vous":"avez parlé"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"parle","ils/elles":"parlent","je":"parle","nous":"parlons","tu":"parles","vous":"parlez"}},"english":"to speak","group":"er","infinitive":"parler","regular":true,"tip":"The pattern for thousands of -er verbs: chop off -er, add -e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent. Learn one, know them all!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"jouera","ils/elles":"joueront","je":"jouerai","nous":"jouerons","tu":"joueras","vous":"jouerez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a joué","ils/elles":"ont joué","je":"ai joué","nous":"avons joué","tu":"as joué","vous":"avez joué"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"joue","ils/elles":"jouent","je":"joue","nous":"jouons","tu":"joues","vous":"jouez"}},"english":"to play","group":"er","infinitive":"jouer","regular":true,"tip":"Same -er pattern as parler. Try swapping in 'aimer' (to like) or 'regarder' (to watch) — same endings!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"mangera","ils/elles":"mangeront","je":"mangerai","nous":"mangerons","tu":"mangeras","vous":"mangerez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a mangé","ils/elles":"ont mangé","je":"ai mangé","nous":"avons mangé","tu":"as mangé","vous":"avez mangé"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"mange","ils/elles":"mangent","je":"mange","nous":"mangeons","tu":"manges","vous":"mangez"}},"english":"to eat","group":"er","infinitive":"manger","regular":true,"tip":"Almost perfectly regular — but 'nous' keeps a sneaky extra e: 'mangeons', so it still sounds soft!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"finira","ils/elles":"finiront","je":"finirai","nous":"finirons","tu":"finiras","vous":"finirez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a fini","ils/elles":"ont fini","je":"ai fini","nous":"avons fini","tu":"as fini","vous":"avez fini"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"finit","ils/elles":"finissent","je":"finis","nous":"finissons","tu":"finis","vous":"finissez"}},"english":"to finish","group":"ir","infinitive":"finir","regular":true,"tip":"The model -ir verb: -is, -is, -it, -issons, -issez, -issent. Spot the double s in the plural forms!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"choisira","ils/elles":"choisiront","je":"choisirai","nous":"choisirons","tu":"choisiras","vous":"choisirez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a choisi","ils/elles":"ont choisi","je":"ai choisi","nous":"avons choisi","tu":"as choisi","vous":"avez choisi"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"choisit","ils/elles":"choisissent","je":"choisis","nous":"choisissons","tu":"choisis","vous":"choisissez"}},"english":"to choose","group":"ir","infinitive":"choisir","regular":true,"tip":"Same -ir pattern as finir. 'Choisir' is a great verb for games — choosing teams, choosing snacks!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"prendra","ils/elles":"prendront","je":"prendrai","nous":"prendrons","tu":"prendras","vous":"prendrez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a pris","ils/elles":"ont pris","je":"ai pris","nous":"avons pris","tu":"as pris","vous":"avez pris"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"prend","ils/elles":"prennent","je":"prends","nous":"prenons","tu":"prends","vous":"prenez"}},"english":"to take","group":"re","infinitive":"prendre","regular":false,"tip":"Tricky one: the stem shrinks in the singular (prend-) and grows in the plural (pren-). Say it out loud!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"mettra","ils/elles":"mettront","je":"mettrai","nous":"mettrons","tu":"mettras","vous":"mettrez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a mis","ils/elles":"ont mis","je":"ai mis","nous":"avons mis","tu":"as mis","vous":"avez mis"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"met","ils/elles":"mettent","je":"mets","nous":"mettons","tu":"mets","vous":"mettez"}},"english":"to put","group":"re","infinitive":"mettre","regular":false,"tip":"Same shrinking-stem trick as prendre: met- in the singular, mett- in the plural."},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"dira","ils/elles":"diront","je":"dirai","nous":"dirons","tu":"diras","vous":"direz"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a dit","ils/elles":"ont dit","je":"ai dit","nous":"avons dit","tu":"as dit","vous":"avez dit"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"dit","ils/elles":"disent","je":"dis","nous":"disons","tu":"dis","vous":"dites"}},"english":"to say","group":"re","infinitive":"dire","regular":false,"tip":"'Vous dites' is the famous oddball — the only -re verb where 'vous' doesn't end in -ez!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"viendra","ils/elles":"viendront","je":"viendrai","nous":"viendrons","tu":"viendras","vous":"viendrez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"est venu","ils/elles":"sont venus","je":"suis venu","nous":"sommes venus","tu":"es venu","vous":"êtes venu"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"vient","ils/elles":"viennent","je":"viens","nous":"venons","tu":"viens","vous":"venez"}},"english":"to come","group":"irregular","infinitive":"venir","regular":false,"tip":"Like aller, venir uses être in the passé composé — and the ending matches who came!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"pourra","ils/elles":"pourront","je":"pourrai","nous":"pourrons","tu":"pourras","vous":"pourrez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a pu","ils/elles":"ont pu","je":"ai pu","nous":"avons pu","tu":"as pu","vous":"avez pu"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"peut","ils/elles":"peuvent","je":"peux","nous":"pouvons","tu":"peux","vous":"pouvez"}},"english":"to be able to, can","group":"irregular","infinitive":"pouvoir","regular":false,"tip":"Super useful: 'je peux' = 'I can'. The futur stem 'pourr-' has a double r — roll it!"},{"conjugations":{"futur":{"il/elle/on":"voudra","ils/elles":"voudront","je":"voudrai","nous":"voudrons","tu":"voudras","vous":"voudrez"},"passe_compose":{"il/elle/on":"a voulu","ils/elles":"ont voulu","je":"ai voulu","nous":"avons voulu","tu":"as voulu","vous":"avez voulu"},"present":{"il/elle/on":"veut","ils/elles":"veulent","je":"veux","nous":"voulons","tu":"veux","vous":"voulez"}},"english":"to want","group":"irregular","infinitive":"vouloir","regular":false,"tip":"Pairs with pouvoir: 'je veux' (I want) + 'je peux' (I can) = you can say almost anything!"}],"version":"2026-10-05"}